<!--
    Dark-mode toggle in the Home header (btnDarkMode).

    Converted from the Figma header icon (118:432). Path data is verbatim
    from the export; the geometry is not redrawn.

    SIZING: the export is a 15.0056x20 leaf; the group maps its 20-unit frame onto
    19.7 units of this 24 viewport — the ink height of ic_notification_bell,
    which is staying and is therefore the fixed reference every other header
    icon is matched to. That also lands within 1.5% of the design's own 20dp
    spec. scale 0.985 with translate (4.6097, 2.15) centres it.

    fillType is deliberately absent: the export carries no fill-rule, so it
    uses non-zero, which is Android's default too. Forcing evenOdd would
    invert the knockouts.

    Same crescent family as the glyph it replaces, but 14% narrower with
    thicker arms (IoU 0.60). This icon carries its own colour: btnDarkMode
    applies no android:tint, and wedora_text_secondary resolves to #9CA3AF in
    dark mode — the exact value the design specifies.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="24"
    android:viewportHeight="24">
    <group
        android:scaleX="0.985"
        android:scaleY="0.985"
        android:translateX="4.6097"
        android:translateY="2.15">
